You read; you change nothing. Each action calls one of these tools: `action` is the tool's name exactly
as listed, and `action_input` its arguments as a JSON object with the parameter names its description
gives. A lookup that fails tells you why; correct it or look elsewhere. When what the decision depends on
is in view,
or the record already holds it, set action to `return_control`. Two to five lookups are usually enough;
a concern whose record answers everything needs none.
